++/* Coachz: a reset keeps a stream's chunks for its next recording instead of freeing all but the last, up to TU_CS_SPARE_CHUNKS and
++ * TU_CS_SPARE_BYTES; past those a chunk is freed as before. A recording of about the size of the one before then allocates nothing: on
++ * Darwin a new chunk is a kernel allocation, a GPU mapping and a CPU view, and k220's render server sometimes sat 20 to 90 ms in one
++ * such CPU view while its encoding queue waited. The command buffer is not pending when it is reset (VkResetCommandBuffer,
++ * vkBeginCommandBuffer, vkResetCommandPool), so nothing the GPU still reads is reused. */
